# Sidecar ADOT (ADR-0010). Traces: OTLP/HTTP da app → X-Ray. Métricas: scrape do /metrics da
# app (127.0.0.1, mesmo network namespace da task) → EMF no CloudWatch Logs.
extensions:
  health_check: {}
receivers:
  otlp:
    protocols:
      http:
        endpoint: 127.0.0.1:4318
  prometheus:
    config:
      scrape_configs:
        - job_name: ${service}
          scrape_interval: 60s
          static_configs:
            - targets: ['127.0.0.1:${metrics_port}']
processors:
  # PERF-21: o collector recusa dados antes de estourar o limite do container.
  memory_limiter:
    check_interval: 1s
    limit_mib: ${memory_limit_mib}
    spike_limit_mib: ${spike_limit_mib}
  batch:
    timeout: 10s
exporters:
  awsxray:
    region: ${region}
    # Vira anotação no X-Ray: busca do trace pelo correlationId (runbook trace-a-transfer).
    indexed_attributes: [app.correlation_id]
  awsemf:
    region: ${region}
    namespace: MiniBanco
    log_group_name: ${metrics_log_group}
    log_stream_name: ${service}
    resource_to_telemetry_conversion:
      enabled: false
    dimension_rollup_option: NoDimensionRollup
    # PERF-25: só o catálogo fechado e só as dimensões de baixa cardinalidade.
    metric_declarations:
      - dimensions: [[reason], [rule], [outcome], []]
        metric_name_selectors: ['^(transfers_|outbox_|fraud_|worker_)']
service:
  extensions: [health_check]
  pipelines:
    traces:
      receivers: [otlp]
      processors: [memory_limiter, batch]
      exporters: [awsxray]
    metrics:
      receivers: [prometheus]
      processors: [memory_limiter, batch]
      exporters: [awsemf]
